---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import BackLink from "../../components/BackLink.astro";

const title = "Slack Setup Guide — Waqtu Resources";
const description =
  "Step-by-step guide to connecting Waqtu with Slack for automatic prayer status updates. Set your status to 'Praying' during prayer times.";
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonical="/resources/slack-setup" ogTitle={title} ogDescription={description}>
  <div class="relative z-10 min-h-screen px-6 py-16 sm:px-10 md:px-14 md:py-24">
    <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
      <BackLink href="/resources" label="Back to Resources" />

      <h1 class="font-display mb-4 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-[var(--waqtu-text)] sm:text-4xl">How to Set Up Slack Status with Waqtu</h1>
      <p class="mb-10 text-[var(--waqtu-muted)] leading-relaxed">
        Follow this guide to connect Waqtu to Slack. Your status will automatically change to &ldquo;Praying&rdquo; during prayer times.
      </p>

      <div class="prose-waqtu">
        <section>
          <h2>1. Open Slack API Console</h2>
          <p>Go to <a href="https://api.slack.com/apps">api.slack.com/apps</a> and sign in with your Slack workspace account.</p>
          <p>Click the green <strong>&ldquo;Create New App&rdquo;</strong> button and select <strong>&ldquo;From scratch.&rdquo;</strong></p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>2. Name Your App</h2>
          <p>Name it something like &ldquo;Waqtu&rdquo; and select your workspace. This name appears in your team&apos;s app directory.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>3. Add Permissions</h2>
          <p>In the left sidebar, navigate to <strong>OAuth &amp; Permissions</strong>.</p>
          <p>Scroll to <strong>Scopes</strong> → <strong>User Token Scopes</strong> → click <strong>Add an OAuth Scope</strong>.</p>
          <p>Search for and add: <code>users.profile:write</code></p>
          <p class="text-sm">This scope allows Waqtu to update YOUR Slack status. It cannot read messages or access channels.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>4. Install to Workspace</h2>
          <p>Scroll up to <strong>OAuth Tokens for Your Workspace</strong> and click <strong>Install to Workspace</strong>.</p>
          <p>Slack will ask you to authorize the app. Click <strong>Allow</strong>.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>5. Copy Your Token</h2>
          <p>After installation, you&apos;ll see a <strong>User OAuth Token</strong> starting with <code>xoxp-</code>.</p>
          <p>Click <strong>Copy</strong> to copy it to your clipboard.</p>
          <blockquote class="text-[var(--waqtu-gold)]">
            ⚠️ Keep this token private. Anyone with this token can update your Slack status.
          </blockquote>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>6. Paste into Waqtu</h2>
          <ol>
            <li>Open Waqtu Settings (click the Waqtu icon → Settings)</li>
            <li>Go to the <strong>Slack</strong> tab</li>
            <li>Paste your token into the &ldquo;User OAuth Token&rdquo; field</li>
            <li>Click <strong>Connect</strong></li>
            <li>Toggle on <strong>Auto-set Slack status</strong></li>
            <li>Customize your status text and emoji if desired</li>
          </ol>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Done!</h2>
          <p>When the next prayer time arrives, Waqtu will automatically set your Slack status. It auto-clears after the prayer block ends — no manual toggling needed.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Troubleshooting</h2>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Status not updating?</strong> — Make sure the token starts with <code>xoxp-</code> (not <code>xoxb-</code> which is a bot token).</li>
            <li><strong>Token rejected?</strong> — Revisit OAuth &amp; Permissions and confirm <code>users.profile:write</code> is listed under User Token Scopes.</li>
            <li><strong>Want to disconnect?</strong> — Click Disconnect in the Slack tab, or revoke the app at api.slack.com/apps.</li>
            <li><strong>Security concern?</strong> — Your token stays in your Mac&apos;s Keychain. Waqtu never transmits it to any server.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-12 neu-card p-6 text-center">
        <p class="font-medium text-[var(--waqtu-text)]">Haven&apos;t downloaded Waqtu yet?</p>
        <a href="/#download" class="neu-btn mt-4 inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-6 py-3 font-medium text-[var(--waqtu-bg)]">Download Waqtu</a>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
